A||||3||contra||How do i fix the front manifold??||||9||
Z||000000||contra||07-10-2000||07:56 AM||||Alright, on my '87 GT i've had a cracked front manifold ever since i bought it. I've checked with Pontiac and they said i've had all the recalls done on the car previously (which i disbelieve since i dont see a heat shield and my rubber strip is still there with the clips and all) <BR>Now, i have 2 sets of good manifolds (front and rear) for the V6. I just need to know how i can replace or even fix my manifold on my GT without too much headache or down time. I really dont feel like paying $550 in labour from a mechanic to take it out and reinstall it. They said they would have to take out all my A/C crap and other things which will take them 10 hours of work at $50 an hour (canadian prices  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>So if anybody knows how i can manage to do it myself, even if it's temporary. I've tried exhaust cement but it keep cracking on me within 2 days.<P>thanx<BR>||||reg||9
Z||000001||My7Fieros||07-10-2000||02:05 PM||||Well, first of all, they're prob. lying about the recalls. If theres no heat shield on the forward (by the rear window) ex. manifold, and that rubber strip is still along the forward decklid edge, then no, all the recalls havnt been done...prob. a lazy mechanic telling you that. <BR>Unfortunantly, should you have to change the forward manifold on your own.....good luck.<BR>Im in the process of doing this on my 87 Gt. All I can say is...ITS A PAIN IN THE A$$!!!!!! I took the decklid off (and anyone who says you dont need to is full a S#%&). 4 bolts and it comes right off, no prob whatsoever. I then laid a long mat over the engine and trunk, and proceeded to lay over the back of the car until my head was smushed up against the rear window. After removing several diff. things, good ole' lucky 13mm wrench came into play taking the manifold off..and LOTS..and LOTS of muscle and patience. Keep this in mind the far right lower bolt is prob. the most difficult bolt on any object in the world to manuever.<BR>After 7 hours of putting a new manifold on last night, Ive pretty much got it on...(once again, that far right lower bolt will give you headaches beyond all belief).<BR>I even had to jack up the car and remove the pivot bolt (and then some)on the A/C compressor just so I could BARELY touch that annoying problem bolt. Anyway you look at it, its a royal pain!!!! But, it can be done. As far as downtime, if youve got 2 days off in a row, do it then...spending EVER minute of it! Good luck! <P>are you really hyped about doing it now? lol<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 07-10-2000).]||||reg||8
Z||000002||contra||07-10-2000||03:21 PM||||took it to this other mechanic today<BR>says he can weld it for me with his mig welder for around $150cdn that includes labour in the price so i might take him up on that<BR>he says he knows a way of getting it out of there (?)<BR>i guess i can't go wrong||||reg||1
